@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of use";
}
<div class="page">
    <main class="page__body" id="main" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="page__inner stack legal" style="max-width:720px">
            <partial name="_Brand" model="(false, false, true)" />
            <a class="back-link" href="/">@Ui.Icon("chevronLeft")Back to Ubuntu Ledger</a>
            <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Last updated 25 October 2026</p>
                <h1 class="page-title">Terms of use</h1>
                <p class="page-sub">The short version: Ubuntu Ledger is a notebook for a lending circle. It keeps the record. It is not a bank and it does not move money.</p>
            </div>

            <section class="stack" style="gap:8px">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Ubuntu Ledger is</h2>
                <p>A shared record of loans and repayments between people who already trust each other. A circle's treasurer records loans. A payment only counts once both the person paying and the person collecting have confirmed it.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="stack" style="gap:8px">
                <h2 class="section-title">What it is not</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>It does not hold, send or receive money. Payments happen between you, by cash or bank transfer.</li>
                    <li>It is not a registered credit provider and does not give financial, credit or legal advice. The interest on a loan is whatever the circle agreed.</li>
                    <li>The ledger is only as accurate as what people record and confirm.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="stack" style="gap:8px">
                <h2 class="section-title">Your part</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Keep your PIN to yourself. What is done with your PIN is treated as done by you.</li>
                    <li>Record and confirm only payments that really happened, with the real amount and date.</li>
                    <li>Do not upload anything that is not a proof of payment, and do not upload other people's information without their permission.</li>
                    <li>Treasurers: you are trusted with other people's records. Use them only to run the circle.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="stack" style="gap:8px">
                <h2 class="section-title">Mistakes and disputes</h2>
                <p>If something is wrong, dispute it or reverse it from inside the app. Entries are never deleted, so the history stays honest. Disagreements about money are settled between the people in the circle; Ubuntu Ledger only shows what each side recorded and confirmed.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="stack" style="gap:8px">
                <h2 class="section-title">The service</h2>
                <p>Ubuntu Ledger is provided as it is, while it is being piloted. We work to keep it available and backed up, but we cannot promise it will never be down or lose data. Keep your own copy of anything important. You can export a loan's ledger as a CSV file at any time. We may change or stop the service, and will tell the circles that use it first.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="stack" style="gap:8px">
                <h2 class="section-title">Your information</h2>
                <p>How we handle personal information is explained in the <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>. By joining a circle you agree to these terms and to that notice.</p>
            </section>

            <p class="small muted">These terms are in plain language for a pilot, governed by the laws of South Africa.</p>
        </div>
    </main>
</div>
